## Article 1 — Definitions

1. **"Software"**: all source code, model weight files, and configurations
published in this repository.
2. **"Personal Use"**: use by any individual or organization for
learning, research, evaluation, or other non-profit purposes, that
generates no direct or indirect revenue and is not performed on
behalf of any commercial entity.
3. **"Commercial Use"**: includes, without limitation:
(1) use of the Software in any product or service that generates revenue;
(2) deployment of the Software on servers, APIs, or SaaS platforms
accessible to third parties;
(3) incorporation of the Software into commercial software, hardware,
or solutions offered or delivered for sale;
(4) use of the Software to provide consulting, implementation, or
customization services to any commercial entity.
4. **"On-Premises Deployment (OPC)"**: deployment of the Software as an
operational service on any server, compute environment, or private
cloud not operated by the Licensor.

## Article 2 — Free Grant

The Licensor hereby grants any individual or organization a free,
non-exclusive, non-transferable license to:

1. download, copy, and modify the Software;
2. run, test, and evaluate the Software for Personal Use;
3. cite and present results from the Software in academic papers and
technical blogs (attribution required).

## Article 3 — Commercial Use Restrictions

**Any Commercial Use requires the Licensor's prior written permission
and payment of a license fee.**
Prior to obtaining such written permission, the licensee shall not:

1. use the Software for any commercial purpose;
2. perform any unauthorized On-Premises Deployment (OPC);
3. deliver, transfer, or sublicense the Software or its Derivative Works
to any third party for commercial purposes.

## Article 4 — Commercial Licensing Process

Commercial licenses are granted on a case-by-case basis. The licensee
must contact the Licensor via:

- Email: Licher255@outlook.com

The Licensor will evaluate and quote based on the use case (industry,
deployment scale, call volume, term, etc.). The license takes effect
upon both parties signing a written agreement.
The Licensor reserves the right to refuse any commercial licensing
request without stating a reason.

## Article 5 — Derivative Works

1. Derivative models produced by fine-tuning, distilling, or quantizing
the Software's model weights, and derivative software based on the
Software, are subject to Article 3 for Commercial Use;
2. Derivative Works created for Personal Use must prominently state
"Derived from open_emby" upon release.

